T_MANIFEST_COVERAGE\", \"N32_WORKBOOK_TERMINALS\") in U.DEFERRED_EDGES\n837\t    assert \"D24_PROVE_EXACT_MANIFEST_COVERAGE\" not in G.binding_inventory()\n838\t    assert \"D24_PROVE_EXACT_MANIFEST_COVERAGE\" in G.full_binding_inventory()\n839\t\n840\t\n841\tdef test_blocked_d91_cannot_reach_d29_yet() -> None:\n842\t    \"\"\"Owned by N30_UNIT_GRAPH: `D91`'s one registered branch predates D29.\n843\t\n844\t    `unit_graph.MODEL_BRANCH_DESTINATIONS[\"D91_CLASSIFY_MODEL_FAILURE\"]` is a\n845\t    frozen 4-tuple that names `D17_CLASSIFY_UNIT_FINDINGS` (the unit repair\n846\t    classifier) but not `D29_CLASSIFY_AND_PLAN_WORKBOOK_REPAIR`. `D91` is a\n847\t    shared bookkeeping node `unit_graph.py` already registers exactly one\n848\t    branch for; this node cannot register a second branch on the same source\n849\t    (every branch on a node fires on each of its executions, so a second,\n850\t    narrower branch would not shadow the first -- it would double-fire and\n851\t    `KeyError` on the first branch's own narrower `ends`), and cannot widen\n852\t    `unit_graph.py`'s table directly (outside this node's write set). A\n853\t    transport failure on `M07`/`M08` that `model_nodes\n854\t    ._repair_destination` classifies as workbook-repairable therefore cannot\n855\t    reach `D29` through the compiled graph in this generation.\n856\t    `D29_CLASSIFY_AND_PLAN_WORKBOOK_REPAIR` itself is fully implemented and\n857\t    independently correct (see the TEST 4/5 cases above, and\n858\t    `model_nodes._repair_destination`'s own routing logic); only the\n859\t    registered graph edge is missing. Closing this is N30_UNIT_GRAPH's\n860\t    `unit_flow_or_denominator` rework edge: add\n861\t    `\"D29_CLASSIFY_AND_PLAN_WORKBOOK_REPAIR\"` to\n862\t    `MODEL_BRANCH_DESTINATIONS[\"D91_CLASSIFY_MODEL_FAILURE\"]`.\n863\t    \"\"\"\n864\t\n865\t    from runtime.langgraph_factory import model_nodes as mn\n866\t\n867\t    assert mn._repair_destination(\"M08_REPAIR_NAMED_WORKBOOK_DEFECT\") == \"D29_CLASSIFY_AND_PLAN_WORKBOOK_REPAIR\""}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5d3513ce-8315-45bf-a456-35d8284d697b","uuid":"3e5fd836-b2c6-4e3b-b1e2-5d34abb1714d","timestamp":"2026-08-12T23:42:44.337Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/filipepinto/Projects/curriculum_builder/.plan26-run/plan26/attempts/N32_WORKBOOK_TERMINALS/attempt-20260812T233231.763782Z-2c5906fec8/repo/tests/runtime/test_plan26_workbook.py","content":"    saver, _connection = G.open_checkpoint_saver(tmp_path / \"out\")\n    compiled = builder.compile(checkpointer=saver, name=G.GRAPH_NAME)\n    assert compiled.name == G.GRAPH_NAME\n\n\ndef test_blocked_d05_cannot_reach_d24_yet() -> None:\n    \"\"\"Owned by N30_UNIT_GRAPH: `D05`'s one registered branch predates D24.\n\n    `unit_graph.UNIT_BRANCHES` registers exactly one conditional-edge branch\n    for `D05_SELECT_NEXT_UNIT`, using `unit_graph.py`'s own frozen\n    `MODEL_BRANCH_DESTINATIONS`-independent fallback\n    (`routing.guard_destinations`), narrowed to `unit_graph.py`'s own\n    `available` argument at registration time. `unit_graph.DEFERRED_EDGES`\n    explicitly declares `(D05_SELECT_NEXT_UNIT, manifest_exhausted, D24_...,\n    N32_WORKBOOK_TERMINALS)` as a row whose destination has no node body --\n    a declaration this node cannot invalidate without either registering a\n    second, colliding branch on the same source (LangGraph raises\n    `ValueError: Branch ... already exists`) or editing `unit_graph.py`\n    itself, which is outside this node's write set. D24 is therefore\n    registered as a real node with real outgoing edges (proven above) but is\n    not yet reachable from `D05` in the compiled graph -- an honest,\n    structural consequence of `binding_inventory()` staying exactly what it\n    was before N32 (see that function's own docstring), not a defect in D24's\n    own implementation. Closing this is N30_UNIT_GRAPH's\n    `unit_flow_or_denominator` rework edge: widen `MODEL_BRANCH_DESTINATIONS`/\n    `UNIT_BRANCHES`' fallback to include `D24_PROVE_EXACT_MANIFEST_COVERAGE`.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    assert (\"D05_SELECT_NEXT_UNIT\", \"manifest_exhausted\", \"D24_PROVE_EXACT_MANIFEST_COVERAGE\", \"N32_WORKBOOK_TERMINALS\") in U.DEFERRED_EDGES\n    assert \"D24_PROVE_EXACT_MANIFEST_COVERAGE\" not in G.binding_inventory()\n    assert \"D24_PROVE_EXACT_MANIFEST_COVERAGE\" in G.full_binding_inventory()\n\n\ndef test_blocked_d91_cannot_reach_d29_yet() -> None:\n    \"\"\"Owned by N30_UNIT_GRAPH: `D91`'s one registered branch predates D29.\n\n    `unit_graph.MODEL_BRANCH_DESTINATIONS[\"D91_CLASSIFY_MODEL_FAILURE\"]` is a\n    frozen 4-tuple that names `D17_CLASSIFY_UNIT_FINDINGS` (the unit repair\n    classifier) but not `D29_CLASSIFY_AND_PLAN_WORKBOOK_REPAIR`. `D91` is a\n    shared bookkeeping node `unit_graph.py` already registers exactly one\n    branch for; this node cannot register a second branch on the same source\n    (every branch on a node fires on each of its executions, so a second,\n    narrower branch would not shadow the first -- it would double-fire and\n    `KeyError` on the first branch's own narrower `ends`), and cannot widen\n    `unit_graph.py`'s table directly (outside this node's write set). A\n    transport failure on `M07`/`M08` that `model_nodes\n    ._repair_destination` classifies as workbook-repairable therefore cannot\n    reach `D29` through the compiled graph in this generation.\n    `D29_CLASSIFY_AND_PLAN_WORKBOOK_REPAIR` itself is fully implemented and\n    independently correct (see the TEST 4/5 cases above, and\n    `model_nodes._repair_destination`'s own routing logic); only the\n    registered graph edge is missing. Closing this is N30_UNIT_GRAPH's\n    `unit_flow_or_denominator` rework edge: add\n    `\"D29_CLASSIFY_AND_PLAN_WORKBOOK_REPAIR\"` to\n    `MODEL_BRANCH_DESTINATIONS[\"D91_CLASSIFY_MODEL_FAILURE\"]`.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    from runtime.langgraph_factory import model_nodes as mn\n\n    assert mn._repair_destination(\"M08_REPAIR_NAMED_WORKBOOK_DEFECT\") == \"D29_CLASSIFY_AND_PLAN_WORKBOOK_REPAIR\"","numLines":60,"startLine":808,"totalLines":869}}}
