{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012rBAeDvm8gEsGgwxHTHr85","type":"tool_result","content":"860\t    (every branch on a node fires on each of its executions, so a second,\n861\t    narrower branch would not shadow the first -- it would double-fire and\n862\t    `KeyError` on the first branch's own narrower `ends`), and cannot widen\n863\t    `unit_graph.py`'s table directly (outside this node's write set). A\n864\t    transport failure on `M07`/`M08` that `model_nodes\n865\t    ._repair_destination` classifies as workbook-repairable therefore cannot\n866\t    reach `D29` through the compiled graph in this generation.\n867\t    `D29_CLASSIFY_AND_PLAN_WORKBOOK_REPAIR` itself is fully implemented and\n868\t    independently correct (see the TEST 4/5 cases above, and\n869\t    `model_nodes._repair_destination`'s own routing logic); only the\n870\t    registered graph edge is missing. Closing this is N30_UNIT_GRAPH's\n871\t    `unit_flow_or_denominator` rework edge: add\n872\t    `\"D29_CLASSIFY_AND_PLAN_WORKBOOK_REPAIR\"` to\n873\t    `MODEL_BRANCH_DESTINATIONS[\"D91_CLASSIFY_MODEL_FAILURE\"]`.\n874\t    \"\"\"\n875\t\n876\t    from runtime.langgraph_factory import model_nodes as mn\n877\t\n878\t    assert mn._repair_destination(\"M08_REPAIR_NAMED_WORKBOOK_DEFECT\") == \"D29_CLASSIFY_AND_PLAN_WORKBOOK_REPAIR\"\n879\t    assert \"D29_CLASSIFY_AND_PLAN_WORKBOOK_REPAIR\" not in U.MODEL_BRANCH_DESTINATIONS[\"D91_CLASSIFY_MODEL_FAILURE\"]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5d3513ce-8315-45bf-a456-35d8284d697b","uuid":"c029a94f-5062-4012-9007-b10e87218245","timestamp":"2026-08-12T23:44:23.567Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/filipepinto/Projects/curriculum_builder/.plan26-run/plan26/attempts/N32_WORKBOOK_TERMINALS/attempt-20260812T233231.763782Z-2c5906fec8/repo/tests/runtime/test_plan26_workbook.py","content":"    (every branch on a node fires on each of its executions, so a second,\n    narrower branch would not shadow the first -- it would double-fire and\n    `KeyError` on the first branch's own narrower `ends`), and cannot widen\n    `unit_graph.py`'s table directly (outside this node's write set). A\n    transport failure on `M07`/`M08` that `model_nodes\n    ._repair_destination` classifies as workbook-repairable therefore cannot\n    reach `D29` through the compiled graph in this generation.\n    `D29_CLASSIFY_AND_PLAN_WORKBOOK_REPAIR` itself is fully implemented and\n    independently correct (see the TEST 4/5 cases above, and\n    `model_nodes._repair_destination`'s own routing logic); only the\n    registered graph edge is missing. Closing this is N30_UNIT_GRAPH's\n    `unit_flow_or_denominator` rework edge: add\n    `\"D29_CLASSIFY_AND_PLAN_WORKBOOK_REPAIR\"` to\n    `MODEL_BRANCH_DESTINATIONS[\"D91_CLASSIFY_MODEL_FAILURE\"]`.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    from runtime.langgraph_factory import model_nodes as mn\n\n    assert mn._repair_destination(\"M08_REPAIR_NAMED_WORKBOOK_DEFECT\") == \"D29_CLASSIFY_AND_PLAN_WORKBOOK_REPAIR\"\n    assert \"D29_CLASSIFY_AND_PLAN_WORKBOOK_REPAIR\" not in U.MODEL_BRANCH_DESTINATIONS[\"D91_CLASSIFY_MODEL_FAILURE\"]","numLines":20,"startLine":860,"totalLines":880}}}
