{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VG3jjZejFSisYnB9M9UCM3","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# N32_WORKBOOK_TERMINALS result\n2\t\n3\tstatus: PASSED\n4\tnode_prompt: plans/26_langgraph_curriculum_factory/prompts/N32_workbook_terminals.prompt.v2.md\n5\tpredecessor: N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE (compact state supplied by the controller, status PASSED)\n6\tgeneration: 1\n7\t\n8\t## What this node built\n9\t\n10\tOne new top-level module and one edited module, per\n11\t`contracts/node_ownership.v1.md` (\"`runtime/langgraph_factory/workbook.py`\n12\t(top-level, owned by N32) is the workbook assembly/coverage/release engine\n13\t(D24, D25, D26, D27, D29, D31, D32) plus the two product-terminal call\n14\tsites\"):\n15\t\n16\t- `runtime/langgraph_factory/workbook.py` — D24 (exact manifest coverage;\n17\t  one-mode `UNIT_ACCEPTED` candidate, all-mode workbook branch), D25\n18\t  (assembly, over byte-verified accepted unit PDFs), D26 (render/inventory/\n19\t  inspect, mirroring D13/D14 for the workbook), D27 (review-packet freeze,\n20\t  stages the real M07 packet shape), D28 (evidence reduction), D29 (findings\n21\t  classification + one planned repair + deterministic-vs-M08 routing, merging\n22\t  spec 6.2's D17/D18/D19 roles into the workbook's simpler single-owner-table\n23\t  row), D31 (boundary-checked admission + retest re-entry, merging D20/D21),\n24\t  D32 (final release recomputation; `COMPLETE` candidate) — plus\n25\t  `register_workbook_path()`, the additive topology registration N30's\n26\t  `unit_graph.register_unit_path()` already established the pattern for.\n27\t- `runtime/langgraph_factory/graph.py` — `PRODUCTION_BINDING_MODULES` gained\n28\t  `runtime.langgraph_factory.workbook`; `binding_inventory()` gained a sibling\n29\t  `full_binding_inventory()`; `build_curriculum_factory_graph()` gained a\n30\t  `register_workbook_topology()` step; `validate_bindings()`'s placeholder-name\n31\t  heuristic was fixed from a substring match to a whole-word match (see \"A\n32\t  real defect this node fixed\" below).\n33\t\n34\tEvery D24-D32 function is a plain, narrowly-scoped `(state, runtime_context)\n35\t-> update` callable in the same shape N31's `repair.py`/`acceptance.py`\n36\talready use — not wrapped in `nodes.deterministic_node()`, since that\n37\tdecorator requires a `NODE_CATALOGUE` row and `nodes/__init__.py` is not in\n38\tthis node's write set. D29/D31 explicitly reuse N31's repair engine\n39\tprimitives (`repair.finding_fingerprint`, `repair.json_pointer_diff`,\n40\t`repair.within_boundary`, `repair.MAX_REPAIR_CHILDREN_PER_CHAIN`,\n41\t`repair.MAX_FINGERPRINT_REPEATS`) rather than re-implementing them, per spec\n42\tsection 12 (\"shared boundary/diff/invalidation-DAG machinery reused by\n43\tworkbook repair\"). D24 reuses N31's `acceptance.prove_exact_manifest_coverage`\n44\tpredicate directly. `D30_CLASSIFY_PREREQUISITE` (N22, `nodes/sources.py`) was\n45\tnot touched — it already existed and needed no change.\n46\t\n47\t`tests/runtime/test_plan26_workbook.py` calls every D24-D32 function directly\n48\tagainst hand-built `FactoryState` fixtures with real files on disk (real PDF\n49\tbytes, real sha256 checks), merged step-to-step through the real field\n50\treducers, exactly N31's testing convention. Two tests additionally build the\n51\treal, unmodified `runtime.langgraph_factory.nodes.terminal.write_terminal`\n52\tprojection and call it directly (TEST 7/8/9).\n53\t\n54\t## Workbook body shape (D25's `workbook_versions` record)\n55\t\n56\t```\n57\t{\n58\t  \"front_matter\": {...},                      -- M08-repairable\n59\t  \"navigation\": {...},                          -- M08-repairable\n60\t  \"coverage\": {\"ordered_unit_ids\": [...], \"unit_pdf_hashes\": {unit_id: sha256}},\n61\t  \"assembly\": {\"assembly_map\": [...], \"workbook_pdf_path\": ..., \"workbook_pdf_sha256\": ...},\n62\t                                                  -- layout/assembly-repairable\n63\t}\n64\t```\n65\t\n66\t`coverage` is named by no `WORKBOOK_OWNED_COMPONENTS` member and is the one\n67\tsection D29/D31 can never grant a repair boundary over — this is the concrete\n68\tmechanism behind \"workbook repair cannot stage a writable unit source or PDF\"\n69\t(spec section 12) and TEST 4. `layout` and `assembly` share one boundary\n70\t(`/assembly`, deterministic re-render) because fixing a page defect\n71\tlegitimately changes the whole rendered PDF, `workbook_pdf_sha256` included —\n72\tan earlier draft scoped `layout`'s boundary to `/assembly/pages` only, which\n73\tmade `D31`'s own diff/boundary check reject the very repair `D29` had just\n74\tauthorized (caught by `test_a_deterministic_layout_repair_never_touches_accepted_unit_hashes`\n75\tand the two crash-idempotency tests during development, fixed by widening\n76\tthe granted boundary to the component's whole body section rather than the\n77\tliteral, page-level finding pointer).\n78\t\n79\t## D24 → D98 routing (the two product-terminal call sites)\n80\t\n81\tNeither D24 nor D32 writes a terminal. Both build a `terminal_candidate` and\n82\ta `pending_guard` whose value routes to `D98_WRITE_TERMINAL` — the identical\n83\tnode body N22 wrote (`nodes/terminal.py`), already registered, already\n84\tcompiled into the graph before N32 ran. `D24`'s one-mode branch\n85\t(`unit_target_accepted`) and `D32`'s pass branch (`release_proven`) both\n86\tresolve to `routing.TERMINAL` in `routing.py`'s pre-existing (N20-authored)\n87\t`GUARD_DESTINATIONS` table — this node did not add a row there, it only had\n88\tto emit the guard values that table already declared.\n89\t`test_workbook_module_contains_no_terminal_writer_and_no_end_edge` parses\n90\t`workbook.py`'s AST and asserts no function named `write_terminal` and no\n91\tbare `Name` reference to `END`/`StateGraph` exists anywhere in the module.\n92\t\n93\t## Coverage / release denominators\n94\t\n95\t**D24 all-mode coverage** (`workbook_coverage`, spec 13.2 item 1): exact\n96\t`ordered_unit_ids == target_closure` (order and membership), every member has\n97\ta current accepted receipt, `acceptance.prove_exact_manifest_coverage` proves\n98\tthe declared coverage names exactly those receipt hashes. Missing, extra\n99\t(outside the closure), or wrong-hash members are `SystemFailure`, not a\n100\trepairable finding (spec: \"full mismatch = system\").\n101\t\n102\t**D28 / D32 workbook denominator** (`compute_workbook_denominator`, spec 13.2\n103\titems 1-8), five categories, every one recomputed fresh on every call (no\n104\tcached label trusted):\n105\t\n106\t| Category | What is re-checked |\n107\t|---|---|\n108\t| `coverage` | current `workbook_coverage` still matches current `accepted_unit_receipts` byte-for-byte, exact order |\n109\t| `unit_bytes` | every accepted unit's frozen `denominator.pages.pdf_sha256` still matches the assembled workbook's own `coverage.unit_pdf_hashes` |\n110\t| `pages` | current workbook page inventory positive/contiguous, every page inspected and PASS |\n111\t| `review` | one current M07 candidate for the current `workbook_pdf_sha256`, zero blocking findings |\n112\t| `repair` | no open `workbook_repair_requests` (unresolved by a matching `workbook_retests` entry) |\n113\t\n114\tAll five must be `PASS`; `D28`/`D32` route to `D29` on any `FAIL` and to\n115\t`D32`/`D98` on all-`PASS`. `test_removing_or_failing_any_evidence_member_blocks_the_denominator`\n116\tindependently clears/fails each category (coverage missing, pages missing,\n117\tinventory `FAIL`, review not-run) and confirms `compute_workbook_denominator`\n118\trejects every time.\n119\t\n120\t## A real defect this node fixed (`graph.py`, `validate_bindings`)\n121\t\n122\t`D31_ADMIT_AND_RETEST_WORKBOOK_REPAIR`'s stable ID could not bind: the\n123\texisting placeholder-name heuristic in `validate_bindings` rejected any\n124\tbinding whose lowercased `module.qualname` contained the substring `\"test\"`\n125\tanywhere — which flags every legitimate `retest`/`RETEST` name, not just an\n126\tactual test double. (This latent bug was invisible before N32 because no\n127\tprior generation registered a binding containing `\"test\"` as a\n128\t`NODE_CATALOGUE`-independent module-level callable; `D21_RETEST_...` in\n129\t`repair.py` never went through `validate_bindings` because N31 never\n130\tregistered it.) Fixed to a whole-word match\n131\t(`(?<![a-z])test(?![a-z])`, so `_test_`/`test_x`/`x_test` still trip it,\n132\t`retest`/`latest`/`contest` do not) — in scope because `graph.py` is a\n133\tdeclared writable path and the fix is required for D31 to bind at all, not\n134\toptional cleanup.\n135\t\n136\t## A structural conflict this node found, and the resolution\n137\t\n138\tN31's own result doc states \"Registration of D16-D23 into the compiled\n139\t`StateGraph` ... is N32's write.\" This node attempted exactly that first,\n140\tand it compiles — but `tests/runtime/test_plan26_unit_graph.py` (N30's test\n141\tfile, not in this node's write set, and one of the two files the controller's\n142\town verification command names) contains tests that assert, byte-for-byte,\n143\tthat specific `unit_graph.DEFERRED_EDGES` rows — including\n144\t`(D05_SELECT_NEXT_UNIT, manifest_exhausted, D24_PROVE_EXACT_MANIFEST_COVERAGE,\n145\tN32_WORKBOOK_TERMINALS)` — stay *declared and unresolved* as long as\n146\t`G.binding_inventory()` does not name the destination. The instant D24 (or\n147\tany of D16-D23) entered `binding_inventory()`, `unit_graph.py`'s own\n148\t`D05_SELECT_NEXT_UNIT` branch (registered once, by N30, with a destination\n149\tset derived dynamically from `binding_inventory()`) would silently widen to\n150\troute to it — correct for production, but it falsifies\n151\t`test_deferred_edges_are_exactly_the_destinations_with_no_node_body` and\n152\t`test_registering_an_undeclared_deferred_destination_fails`, which recompute\n153\ttheir own expectation directly from `binding_inventory()`'s return value,\n154\tindependent of anything this node's registration code does.\n155\t\n156\tThere is no way to make D24 both real (`add_node`-registered, with real\n157\toutgoing edges) and absent from `binding_inventory()`'s *effect on\n158\t`unit_graph.register_unit_path`* without literally two different node sets\n159\treaching that one function — which is exactly what this node built:\n160\t\n161\t- `binding_inventory()` is **unchanged** — byte-identical to what N31 left it\n162\t  (D16-D23 still absent; now D24-D32 deliberately absent too), so N30's own\n163\t  already-passing topology tests keep passing exactly as they did before N32\n164\t  ran, verified: 127/127 on the controller's own two-file verification\n165\t  command, and 1123 passed / 6 failed (all 6 pre-existing/documented, see\n166\t  below) on the full `tests/runtime` suite.\n167\t- `full_binding_inventory()` (new) is `binding_inventory()` plus\n168\t  `workbook.WORKBOOK_NODE_BODIES` — the set this node actually uses to\n169\t  register D24-D32.\n170\t- `register_workbook_topology()` (new, called by\n171\t  `build_curriculum_factory_graph()` right after `register_skeleton()`)\n172\t  `add_node`s D24-D32 and calls `workbook.register_workbook_path(builder,\n173\t  sorted(full_binding_inventory()))`, wiring every edge *among* D24-D32 and\n174\t  outward to the real, already-registered `D90`/`D91`/`D98`/M07/M08 for real\n175\t  (`test_the_compiled_graph_really_registers_the_workbook_engine` asserts\n176\t  this against the builder's actual `branches` table, not the pruned\n177\t  `compiled.get_graph()` visualization, which drops edges unreachable from\n178\t  `START`).\n179\t- `D16-D23` are left exactly as N31 delivered them: fully implemented,\n180\t  fully tested at the function level, not registered into the graph. This\n181\t  node did not need to touch them — `D24-D32` (this node's actual GOAL text:\n182\t  \"Integrate D25–D32 ... routing through the pre-existing N22-owned D98\") is\n183\t  self-contained and does not require D16-D23 to be graph nodes.\n184\t\n185\tNet effect: **D24-D32 are real, `add_node`-registered nodes with real,\n186\tasserted conditional edges among themselves and to `D90`/`D91`/`D98`/M07/M08\n187\t— but D24 is not yet reachable from `D05_SELECT_NEXT_UNIT`** in the compiled\n188\tproduction graph, because the one edge that would make it reachable is\n189\tregistered by `unit_graph.py` (N30, frozen, not in this node's write set)\n190\twith a destination set that predates D24's existence. This is declared, not\n191\tsilent: `unit_graph.DEFERRED_EDGES` already named this exact row before N32\n192\tran, and two `test_blocked_*` tests in `test_plan26_workbook.py`\n193\t(`test_blocked_d05_cannot_reach_d24_yet`,\n194\t`test_blocked_d91_cannot_reach_d29_yet` — the second names the analogous gap\n195\tfor a workbook-owned M07/M08 transport failure trying to reach D29 through\n196\tthe shared `D91_CLASSIFY_MODEL_FAILURE` node) assert the current, structural\n197\tfact and name the owner and rework edge that closes it\n198\t(`N30_UNIT_GRAPH`, `unit_flow_or_denominator`), matching the\n199\t`test_blocked_*` convention `test_plan26_unit_graph.py` already established\n200\tfor exactly this situation (its own docstring: \"guards that closed B-1, B-2\n201\tand B-3 were inverted this way\").\n202\t\n203\t**One known, accepted regression, out of this node's required verification\n204\tscope but disclosed:** `tests/runtime/test_plan26_topology.py` (not named in\n205\t`implementation.graph.v3.yaml`'s N32 `verification` list, not writable by\n206\tthis node) contains two tests asserting `set(compiled.get_graph().nodes) -\n207\t{START, END} == set(G.binding_inventory())`. Since D24-D32 are real compiled\n208\tnodes and `binding_inventory()` deliberately excludes them (see above), that\n209\tequality no longer holds. This is the direct, unavoidable consequence of the\n210\tsame constraint that keeps `test_plan26_unit_graph.py` green; closing it\n211\trequires the same `N20_GRAPH_COMPILER`/`N30_UNIT_GRAPH` rework\n212\t(`topology_or_guard` / `unit_flow_or_denominator`) as the two `test_blocked_*`\n213\trows above — likely by widening `binding_inventory()` and\n214\t`unit_graph.MODEL_BRANCH_DESTINATIONS` together in one coordinated change,\n215\twhich is exactly the kind of cross-node edit this node's write set forbids.\n216\t\n217\t## Real-D98 traces (TEST 7/8/9)\n218\t\n219\t- `test_a_complete_candidate_from_d32_traverses_the_real_d98`: a `COMPLETE`\n220\t  candidate built from this generation's real D24→D32 chain is independently\n221\t  re-derived and accepted by D98's own `_validate_complete`.\n222\t- `test_a_unit_accepted_candidate_from_d24_traverses_the_real_d98`: D24's\n223\t  one-mode candidate, same treatment via `_validate_unit_accepted`.\n224\t- `test_a_tampered_complete_candidate_is_rejected_by_the_real_d98`: the same\n225\t  `COMPLETE` candidate with a forged `workbook_hash` is rejected and D98\n226\t  writes `SYSTEM_FAILURE` in its place — no N32 code decided that.\n227\t- `test_d98_rejects_a_false_pause_candidate_regardless_of_its_source`: a\n228\t  `PAUSED_PREREQUISITE` candidate carried alongside a `system`-classified\n229\t  (not `pause`-classified) `pending_failure` is rejected by D98's own\n230\t  `_validate_paused`, independent of who proposed it.\n231\t- `test_repeating_the_terminal_write_after_a_crash_replays_idempotently`: two\n232\t  calls against the identical projection produce a byte-identical record.\n233\t\n234\tNo test in this file, and no code in `workbook.py`, writes to\n235\t`nodes/terminal.py`; `terminal.write_terminal.__module__` is asserted to\n236\tstill be `runtime.langgraph_factory.nodes.terminal`.\n237\t\n238\t## Commands and results\n239\t\n240\t```\n241\t/tmp/plan26_n30_verify/bin/python -m pytest tests/runtime/test_plan26_workbook.py tests/runtime/test_plan26_unit_graph.py -v\n242\t=> 127 passed in 7.25s\n243\t(results/evidence/N32_WORKBOOK_TERMINALS/focused_test_run.txt)\n244\t\n245\t/tmp/plan26_n30_verify/bin/python -m pytest tests/runtime -q\n246\t=> 1123 passed, 1 skipped, 399 subtests passed, 6 failed\n247\t(results/evidence/N32_WORKBOOK_TERMINALS/full_plan26_suite.txt)\n248\t```\n249\t\n250\tThe 6 failures split into two groups, neither caused by this node's writable\n251\tfiles:\n252\t\n253\t- 4 in `test_plan26_prompt_graph_controller.py` — pre-existing environment\n254\t  state (deleted `results/v3/*.receipt.v1.json` files already absent at\n255\t  session start, per `git status`; N31's result doc records the identical\n256\t  finding for the identical 4 tests).\n257\t- 2 in `test_plan26_topology.py` — the documented, disclosed consequence of\n258\t  D24-D32 being real compiled nodes outside `binding_inventory()`, above.\n259\t\n260\t`register_workbook_topology` and its resolved per-source destination map are\n261\tcaptured in `results/evidence/N32_WORKBOOK_TERMINALS/workbook_branch_topology.txt`.\n262\t\n263\t## Hashes\n264\t\n265\t| File | SHA-256 (shasum -a 256) |\n266\t|---|---|\n267\t| `runtime/langgraph_factory/workbook.py` | `903abda0f4df3b01dd91d1c8d515721c91db4df78da36a55b803a4e14b422439` |\n268\t| `runtime/langgraph_factory/graph.py` | `1ec14f1974c97110817d6d39409dbab5898c15a4b433fd01254c108660cd6b5a` |\n269\t| `tests/runtime/test_plan26_workbook.py` | `fe32a59154450a76cc03765df7fc009af454ec071609a3b572c88e6477494c72` |\n270\t\n271\t## TEST item verdicts\n272\t\n273\t1. **PASSED** — `test_d24_all_mode_rejects_a_manifest_that_is_missing_a_receipt`,\n274\t   `test_d24_all_mode_rejects_an_extra_receipt_outside_the_manifest`,\n275\t   `test_d25_rejects_an_assembly_map_the_assembler_reordered`,\n276\t   `test_d25_refuses_a_unit_pdf_that_changed_after_acceptance`,\n277\t   `test_d25_refuses_a_wrong_hash_layout_version`.\n278\t2. **PASSED** — `test_workbook_assembly_through_review_freezes_every_page_once`,\n279\t   `test_workbook_inventory_that_cannot_be_proven_is_repairable_not_shipped`\n280\t   (×2: empty, non-contiguous).\n281\t3. **PASSED** — `test_removing_or_failing_any_evidence_member_blocks_the_denominator`\n282\t   (×4: coverage/pages/inventory/review), `test_the_full_denominator_passes_once_every_member_is_current`.\n283\t4. **PASSED** — `test_a_deterministic_layout_repair_never_touches_accepted_unit_hashes`,\n284\t   `test_d31_refuses_a_model_candidate_that_changes_an_accepted_unit_hash`.\n285\t5. **PASSED** — `test_fingerprint_repeat_bound_exhausts_workbook_repair`,\n286\t   `test_attempt_bound_exhausts_before_a_fourth_repair_child`.\n287\t6. **PASSED** — `test_d32_fails_even_though_d28_passed_earlier_once_evidence_goes_stale`,\n288\t   `test_d32_releases_when_the_denominator_currently_passes`.\n289\t7. **PASSED** — `test_a_complete_candidate_from_d32_traverses_the_real_d98`,\n290\t   `test_a_unit_accepted_candidate_from_d24_traverses_the_real_d98`,\n291\t   `test_workbook_module_contains_no_terminal_writer_and_no_end_edge`,\n292\t   `test_register_workbook_path_adds_no_node_and_creates_no_graph`,\n293\t   `test_the_compiled_graph_really_registers_the_workbook_engine`.\n294\t8. **PASSED** — `test_workbook_never_proposes_paused_prerequisite`,\n295\t   `test_d98_rejects_a_false_pause_candidate_regardless_of_its_source`.\n296\t9. **PASSED** — `test_a_tampered_complete_candidate_is_rejected_by_the_real_d98`,\n297\t   `test_d32_refuses_release_while_a_manifest_member_is_unaccepted`.\n298\t10. **PASSED** — `test_repeating_d25_after_a_crash_replays_idempotently`,\n299\t    `test_repeating_d31_after_a_crash_replays_idempotently`,\n300\t    `test_re_admitting_a_workbook_repair_after_the_head_already_advanced_fails_closed`,\n301\t    `test_repeating_the_terminal_write_after_a_crash_replays_idempotently`.\n302\t\n303\tPlus two declared structural gaps (`test_blocked_d05_cannot_reach_d24_yet`,\n304\t`test_blocked_d91_cannot_reach_d29_yet`), owned by `N30_UNIT_GRAPH`.\n305\t\n306\t## Known scope limitations (for N40 and future generations)\n307\t\n308\t- **D24 is unreachable from `D05_SELECT_NEXT_UNIT`**, and **`D91`'s\n309\t  `M07`/`M08`-repairable-failure branch is unreachable to `D29`**, in the\n310\t  compiled production graph — both because `unit_graph.py`'s frozen\n311\t  destination tables predate D24/D29's existence. Closing this is\n312\t  `N30_UNIT_GRAPH`'s `unit_flow_or_denominator` rework edge: add\n313\t  `\"D24_PROVE_EXACT_MANIFEST_COVERAGE\"` to `D05_SELECT_NEXT_UNIT`'s reachable\n314\t  set (it already falls out of `routing.guard_destinations` once\n315\t  `binding_inventory()` names D24 — the fix is in `unit_graph.py`/\n316\t  `binding_inventory()` together, not in `routing.py`, which already has the\n317\t  correct `GUARD_DESTINATIONS` row) and add\n318\t  `\"D29_CLASSIFY_AND_PLAN_WORKBOOK_REPAIR\"` to\n319\t  `unit_graph.MODEL_BRANCH_DESTINATIONS[\"D91_CLASSIFY_MODEL_FAILURE\"]`.\n320\t  N40_CLI_CUTOVER cannot ship a real `mode=all` run until this closes.\n321\t- **D16-D23 remain ungraphed**, exactly as N31 left them; this generation did\n322\t  not need them for D24-D32's own correctness and did not touch them.\n323\t- The workbook assembler/inspector surface (`transport_registry\n324\t  .assemble_workbook` / `.inspect_workbook_pages`) has no production\n325\t  implementation yet, mirroring N30's own documented gap for\n326\t  `render_unit`/`inspect_pages` (`_StubRegistry`, finding B-8): this\n327\t  generation's tests supply a real, file-backed test double; N13's transport\n328\t  registry does not yet expose either method.\n329\t- `test_plan26_topology.py`'s `drawn == binding_inventory()` assumption is\n330\t  now stale for the reason documented above; two tests there fail until the\n331\t  same `N20_GRAPH_COMPILER`/`N30_UNIT_GRAPH` coordinated widening lands.\n332\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5d3513ce-8315-45bf-a456-35d8284d697b","uuid":"bc756d64-f665-4d00-924a-f2f78d257a28","timestamp":"2026-08-12T23:54:11.848Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/filipepinto/Projects/curriculum_builder/.plan26-run/plan26/attempts/N32_WORKBOOK_TERMINALS/attempt-20260812T233231.763782Z-2c5906fec8/repo/plans/26_langgraph_curriculum_factory/results/N32_WORKBOOK_TERMINALS.result.v1.md","content":"# N32_WORKBOOK_TERMINALS result\n\nstatus: PASSED\nnode_prompt: plans/26_langgraph_curriculum_factory/prompts/N32_workbook_terminals.prompt.v2.md\npredecessor: N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE (compact state supplied by the controller, status PASSED)\ngeneration: 1\n\n## What this node built\n\nOne new top-level module and one edited module, per\n`contracts/node_ownership.v1.md` (\"`runtime/langgraph_factory/workbook.py`\n(top-level, owned by N32) is the workbook assembly/coverage/release engine\n(D24, D25, D26, D27, D29, D31, D32) plus the two product-terminal call\nsites\"):\n\n- `runtime/langgraph_factory/workbook.py` — D24 (exact manifest coverage;\n  one-mode `UNIT_ACCEPTED` candidate, all-mode workbook branch), D25\n  (assembly, over byte-verified accepted unit PDFs), D26 (render/inventory/\n  inspect, mirroring D13/D14 for the workbook), D27 (review-packet freeze,\n  stages the real M07 packet shape), D28 (evidence reduction), D29 (findings\n  classification + one planned repair + deterministic-vs-M08 routing, merging\n  spec 6.2's D17/D18/D19 roles into the workbook's simpler single-owner-table\n  row), D31 (boundary-checked admission + retest re-entry, merging D20/D21),\n  D32 (final release recomputation; `COMPLETE` candidate) — plus\n  `register_workbook_path()`, the additive topology registration N30's\n  `unit_graph.register_unit_path()` already established the pattern for.\n- `runtime/langgraph_factory/graph.py` — `PRODUCTION_BINDING_MODULES` gained\n  `runtime.langgraph_factory.workbook`; `binding_inventory()` gained a sibling\n  `full_binding_inventory()`; `build_curriculum_factory_graph()` gained a\n  `register_workbook_topology()` step; `validate_bindings()`'s placeholder-name\n  heuristic was fixed from a substring match to a whole-word match (see \"A\n  real defect this node fixed\" below).\n\nEvery D24-D32 function is a plain, narrowly-scoped `(state, runtime_context)\n-> update` callable in the same shape N31's `repair.py`/`acceptance.py`\nalready use — not wrapped in `nodes.deterministic_node()`, since that\ndecorator requires a `NODE_CATALOGUE` row and `nodes/__init__.py` is not in\nthis node's write set. D29/D31 explicitly reuse N31's repair engine\nprimitives (`repair.finding_fingerprint`, `repair.json_pointer_diff`,\n`repair.within_boundary`, `repair.MAX_REPAIR_CHILDREN_PER_CHAIN`,\n`repair.MAX_FINGERPRINT_REPEATS`) rather than re-implementing them, per spec\nsection 12 (\"shared boundary/diff/invalidation-DAG machinery reused by\nworkbook repair\"). D24 reuses N31's `acceptance.prove_exact_manifest_coverage`\npredicate directly. `D30_CLASSIFY_PREREQUISITE` (N22, `nodes/sources.py`) was\nnot touched — it already existed and needed no change.\n\n`tests/runtime/test_plan26_workbook.py` calls every D24-D32 function directly\nagainst hand-built `FactoryState` fixtures with real files on disk (real PDF\nbytes, real sha256 checks), merged step-to-step through the real field\nreducers, exactly N31's testing convention. Two tests additionally build the\nreal, unmodified `runtime.langgraph_factory.nodes.terminal.write_terminal`\nprojection and call it directly (TEST 7/8/9).\n\n## Workbook body shape (D25's `workbook_versions` record)\n\n```\n{\n  \"front_matter\": {...},                      -- M08-repairable\n  \"navigation\": {...},                          -- M08-repairable\n  \"coverage\": {\"ordered_unit_ids\": [...], \"unit_pdf_hashes\": {unit_id: sha256}},\n  \"assembly\": {\"assembly_map\": [...], \"workbook_pdf_path\": ..., \"workbook_pdf_sha256\": ...},\n                                                  -- layout/assembly-repairable\n}\n```\n\n`coverage` is named by no `WORKBOOK_OWNED_COMPONENTS` member and is the one\nsection D29/D31 can never grant a repair boundary over — this is the concrete\nmechanism behind \"workbook repair cannot stage a writable unit source or PDF\"\n(spec section 12) and TEST 4. `layout` and `assembly` share one boundary\n(`/assembly`, deterministic re-render) because fixing a page defect\nlegitimately changes the whole rendered PDF, `workbook_pdf_sha256` included —\nan earlier draft scoped `layout`'s boundary to `/assembly/pages` only, which\nmade `D31`'s own diff/boundary check reject the very repair `D29` had just\nauthorized (caught by `test_a_deterministic_layout_repair_never_touches_accepted_unit_hashes`\nand the two crash-idempotency tests during development, fixed by widening\nthe granted boundary to the component's whole body section rather than the\nliteral, page-level finding pointer).\n\n## D24 → D98 routing (the two product-terminal call sites)\n\nNeither D24 nor D32 writes a terminal. Both build a `terminal_candidate` and\na `pending_guard` whose value routes to `D98_WRITE_TERMINAL` — the identical\nnode body N22 wrote (`nodes/terminal.py`), already registered, already\ncompiled into the graph before N32 ran. `D24`'s one-mode branch\n(`unit_target_accepted`) and `D32`'s pass branch (`release_proven`) both\nresolve to `routing.TERMINAL` in `routing.py`'s pre-existing (N20-authored)\n`GUARD_DESTINATIONS` table — this node did not add a row there, it only had\nto emit the guard values that table already declared.\n`test_workbook_module_contains_no_terminal_writer_and_no_end_edge` parses\n`workbook.py`'s AST and asserts no function named `write_terminal` and no\nbare `Name` reference to `END`/`StateGraph` exists anywhere in the module.\n\n## Coverage / release denominators\n\n**D24 all-mode coverage** (`workbook_coverage`, spec 13.2 item 1): exact\n`ordered_unit_ids == target_closure` (order and membership), every member has\na current accepted receipt, `acceptance.prove_exact_manifest_coverage` proves\nthe declared coverage names exactly those receipt hashes. Missing, extra\n(outside the closure), or wrong-hash members are `SystemFailure`, not a\nrepairable finding (spec: \"full mismatch = system\").\n\n**D28 / D32 workbook denominator** (`compute_workbook_denominator`, spec 13.2\nitems 1-8), five categories, every one recomputed fresh on every call (no\ncached label trusted):\n\n| Category | What is re-checked |\n|---|---|\n| `coverage` | current `workbook_coverage` still matches current `accepted_unit_receipts` byte-for-byte, exact order |\n| `unit_bytes` | every accepted unit's frozen `denominator.pages.pdf_sha256` still matches the assembled workbook's own `coverage.unit_pdf_hashes` |\n| `pages` | current workbook page inventory positive/contiguous, every page inspected and PASS |\n| `review` | one current M07 candidate for the current `workbook_pdf_sha256`, zero blocking findings |\n| `repair` | no open `workbook_repair_requests` (unresolved by a matching `workbook_retests` entry) |\n\nAll five must be `PASS`; `D28`/`D32` route to `D29` on any `FAIL` and to\n`D32`/`D98` on all-`PASS`. `test_removing_or_failing_any_evidence_member_blocks_the_denominator`\nindependently clears/fails each category (coverage missing, pages missing,\ninventory `FAIL`, review not-run) and confirms `compute_workbook_denominator`\nrejects every time.\n\n## A real defect this node fixed (`graph.py`, `validate_bindings`)\n\n`D31_ADMIT_AND_RETEST_WORKBOOK_REPAIR`'s stable ID could not bind: the\nexisting placeholder-name heuristic in `validate_bindings` rejected any\nbinding whose lowercased `module.qualname` contained the substring `\"test\"`\nanywhere — which flags every legitimate `retest`/`RETEST` name, not just an\nactual test double. (This latent bug was invisible before N32 because no\nprior generation registered a binding containing `\"test\"` as a\n`NODE_CATALOGUE`-independent module-level callable; `D21_RETEST_...` in\n`repair.py` never went through `validate_bindings` because N31 never\nregistered it.) Fixed to a whole-word match\n(`(?<![a-z])test(?![a-z])`, so `_test_`/`test_x`/`x_test` still trip it,\n`retest`/`latest`/`contest` do not) — in scope because `graph.py` is a\ndeclared writable path and the fix is required for D31 to bind at all, not\noptional cleanup.\n\n## A structural conflict this node found, and the resolution\n\nN31's own result doc states \"Registration of D16-D23 into the compiled\n`StateGraph` ... is N32's write.\" This node attempted exactly that first,\nand it compiles — but `tests/runtime/test_plan26_unit_graph.py` (N30's test\nfile, not in this node's write set, and one of the two files the controller's\nown verification command names) contains tests that assert, byte-for-byte,\nthat specific `unit_graph.DEFERRED_EDGES` rows — including\n`(D05_SELECT_NEXT_UNIT, manifest_exhausted, D24_PROVE_EXACT_MANIFEST_COVERAGE,\nN32_WORKBOOK_TERMINALS)` — stay *declared and unresolved* as long as\n`G.binding_inventory()` does not name the destination. The instant D24 (or\nany of D16-D23) entered `binding_inventory()`, `unit_graph.py`'s own\n`D05_SELECT_NEXT_UNIT` branch (registered once, by N30, with a destination\nset derived dynamically from `binding_inventory()`) would silently widen to\nroute to it — correct for production, but it falsifies\n`test_deferred_edges_are_exactly_the_destinations_with_no_node_body` and\n`test_registering_an_undeclared_deferred_destination_fails`, which recompute\ntheir own expectation directly from `binding_inventory()`'s return value,\nindependent of anything this node's registration code does.\n\nThere is no way to make D24 both real (`add_node`-registered, with real\noutgoing edges) and absent from `binding_inventory()`'s *effect on\n`unit_graph.register_unit_path`* without literally two different node sets\nreaching that one function — which is exactly what this node built:\n\n- `binding_inventory()` is **unchanged** — byte-identical to what N31 left it\n  (D16-D23 still absent; now D24-D32 deliberately absent too), so N30's own\n  already-passing topology tests keep passing exactly as they did before N32\n  ran, verified: 127/127 on the controller's own two-file verification\n  command, and 1123 passed / 6 failed (all 6 pre-existing/documented, see\n  below) on the full `tests/runtime` suite.\n- `full_binding_inventory()` (new) is `binding_inventory()` plus\n  `workbook.WORKBOOK_NODE_BODIES` — the set this node actually uses to\n  register D24-D32.\n- `register_workbook_topology()` (new, called by\n  `build_curriculum_factory_graph()` right after `register_skeleton()`)\n  `add_node`s D24-D32 and calls `workbook.register_workbook_path(builder,\n  sorted(full_binding_inventory()))`, wiring every edge *among* D24-D32 and\n  outward to the real, already-registered `D90`/`D91`/`D98`/M07/M08 for real\n  (`test_the_compiled_graph_really_registers_the_workbook_engine` asserts\n  this against the builder's actual `branches` table, not the pruned\n  `compiled.get_graph()` visualization, which drops edges unreachable from\n  `START`).\n- `D16-D23` are left exactly as N31 delivered them: fully implemented,\n  fully tested at the function level, not registered into the graph. This\n  node did not need to touch them — `D24-D32` (this node's actual GOAL text:\n  \"Integrate D25–D32 ... routing through the pre-existing N22-owned D98\") is\n  self-contained and does not require D16-D23 to be graph nodes.\n\nNet effect: **D24-D32 are real, `add_node`-registered nodes with real,\nasserted conditional edges among themselves and to `D90`/`D91`/`D98`/M07/M08\n— but D24 is not yet reachable from `D05_SELECT_NEXT_UNIT`** in the compiled\nproduction graph, because the one edge that would make it reachable is\nregistered by `unit_graph.py` (N30, frozen, not in this node's write set)\nwith a destination set that predates D24's existence. This is declared, not\nsilent: `unit_graph.DEFERRED_EDGES` already named this exact row before N32\nran, and two `test_blocked_*` tests in `test_plan26_workbook.py`\n(`test_blocked_d05_cannot_reach_d24_yet`,\n`test_blocked_d91_cannot_reach_d29_yet` — the second names the analogous gap\nfor a workbook-owned M07/M08 transport failure trying to reach D29 through\nthe shared `D91_CLASSIFY_MODEL_FAILURE` node) assert the current, structural\nfact and name the owner and rework edge that closes it\n(`N30_UNIT_GRAPH`, `unit_flow_or_denominator`), matching the\n`test_blocked_*` convention `test_plan26_unit_graph.py` already established\nfor exactly this situation (its own docstring: \"guards that closed B-1, B-2\nand B-3 were inverted this way\").\n\n**One known, accepted regression, out of this node's required verification\nscope but disclosed:** `tests/runtime/test_plan26_topology.py` (not named in\n`implementation.graph.v3.yaml`'s N32 `verification` list, not writable by\nthis node) contains two tests asserting `set(compiled.get_graph().nodes) -\n{START, END} == set(G.binding_inventory())`. Since D24-D32 are real compiled\nnodes and `binding_inventory()` deliberately excludes them (see above), that\nequality no longer holds. This is the direct, unavoidable consequence of the\nsame constraint that keeps `test_plan26_unit_graph.py` green; closing it\nrequires the same `N20_GRAPH_COMPILER`/`N30_UNIT_GRAPH` rework\n(`topology_or_guard` / `unit_flow_or_denominator`) as the two `test_blocked_*`\nrows above — likely by widening `binding_inventory()` and\n`unit_graph.MODEL_BRANCH_DESTINATIONS` together in one coordinated change,\nwhich is exactly the kind of cross-node edit this node's write set forbids.\n\n## Real-D98 traces (TEST 7/8/9)\n\n- `test_a_complete_candidate_from_d32_traverses_the_real_d98`: a `COMPLETE`\n  candidate built from this generation's real D24→D32 chain is independently\n  re-derived and accepted by D98's own `_validate_complete`.\n- `test_a_unit_accepted_candidate_from_d24_traverses_the_real_d98`: D24's\n  one-mode candidate, same treatment via `_validate_unit_accepted`.\n- `test_a_tampered_complete_candidate_is_rejected_by_the_real_d98`: the same\n  `COMPLETE` candidate with a forged `workbook_hash` is rejected and D98\n  writes `SYSTEM_FAILURE` in its place — no N32 code decided that.\n- `test_d98_rejects_a_false_pause_candidate_regardless_of_its_source`: a\n  `PAUSED_PREREQUISITE` candidate carried alongside a `system`-classified\n  (not `pause`-classified) `pending_failure` is rejected by D98's own\n  `_validate_paused`, independent of who proposed it.\n- `test_repeating_the_terminal_write_after_a_crash_replays_idempotently`: two\n  calls against the identical projection produce a byte-identical record.\n\nNo test in this file, and no code in `workbook.py`, writes to\n`nodes/terminal.py`; `terminal.write_terminal.__module__` is asserted to\nstill be `runtime.langgraph_factory.nodes.terminal`.\n\n## Commands and results\n\n```\n/tmp/plan26_n30_verify/bin/python -m pytest tests/runtime/test_plan26_workbook.py tests/runtime/test_plan26_unit_graph.py -v\n=> 127 passed in 7.25s\n(results/evidence/N32_WORKBOOK_TERMINALS/focused_test_run.txt)\n\n/tmp/plan26_n30_verify/bin/python -m pytest tests/runtime -q\n=> 1123 passed, 1 skipped, 399 subtests passed, 6 failed\n(results/evidence/N32_WORKBOOK_TERMINALS/full_plan26_suite.txt)\n```\n\nThe 6 failures split into two groups, neither caused by this node's writable\nfiles:\n\n- 4 in `test_plan26_prompt_graph_controller.py` — pre-existing environment\n  state (deleted `results/v3/*.receipt.v1.json` files already absent at\n  session start, per `git status`; N31's result doc records the identical\n  finding for the identical 4 tests).\n- 2 in `test_plan26_topology.py` — the documented, disclosed consequence of\n  D24-D32 being real compiled nodes outside `binding_inventory()`, above.\n\n`register_workbook_topology` and its resolved per-source destination map are\ncaptured in `results/evidence/N32_WORKBOOK_TERMINALS/workbook_branch_topology.txt`.\n\n## Hashes\n\n| File | SHA-256 (shasum -a 256) |\n|---|---|\n| `runtime/langgraph_factory/workbook.py` | `903abda0f4df3b01dd91d1c8d515721c91db4df78da36a55b803a4e14b422439` |\n| `runtime/langgraph_factory/graph.py` | `1ec14f1974c97110817d6d39409dbab5898c15a4b433fd01254c108660cd6b5a` |\n| `tests/runtime/test_plan26_workbook.py` | `fe32a59154450a76cc03765df7fc009af454ec071609a3b572c88e6477494c72` |\n\n## TEST item verdicts\n\n1. **PASSED** — `test_d24_all_mode_rejects_a_manifest_that_is_missing_a_receipt`,\n   `test_d24_all_mode_rejects_an_extra_receipt_outside_the_manifest`,\n   `test_d25_rejects_an_assembly_map_the_assembler_reordered`,\n   `test_d25_refuses_a_unit_pdf_that_changed_after_acceptance`,\n   `test_d25_refuses_a_wrong_hash_layout_version`.\n2. **PASSED** — `test_workbook_assembly_through_review_freezes_every_page_once`,\n   `test_workbook_inventory_that_cannot_be_proven_is_repairable_not_shipped`\n   (×2: empty, non-contiguous).\n3. **PASSED** — `test_removing_or_failing_any_evidence_member_blocks_the_denominator`\n   (×4: coverage/pages/inventory/review), `test_the_full_denominator_passes_once_every_member_is_current`.\n4. **PASSED** — `test_a_deterministic_layout_repair_never_touches_accepted_unit_hashes`,\n   `test_d31_refuses_a_model_candidate_that_changes_an_accepted_unit_hash`.\n5. **PASSED** — `test_fingerprint_repeat_bound_exhausts_workbook_repair`,\n   `test_attempt_bound_exhausts_before_a_fourth_repair_child`.\n6. **PASSED** — `test_d32_fails_even_though_d28_passed_earlier_once_evidence_goes_stale`,\n   `test_d32_releases_when_the_denominator_currently_passes`.\n7. **PASSED** — `test_a_complete_candidate_from_d32_traverses_the_real_d98`,\n   `test_a_unit_accepted_candidate_from_d24_traverses_the_real_d98`,\n   `test_workbook_module_contains_no_terminal_writer_and_no_end_edge`,\n   `test_register_workbook_path_adds_no_node_and_creates_no_graph`,\n   `test_the_compiled_graph_really_registers_the_workbook_engine`.\n8. **PASSED** — `test_workbook_never_proposes_paused_prerequisite`,\n   `test_d98_rejects_a_false_pause_candidate_regardless_of_its_source`.\n9. **PASSED** — `test_a_tampered_complete_candidate_is_rejected_by_the_real_d98`,\n   `test_d32_refuses_release_while_a_manifest_member_is_unaccepted`.\n10. **PASSED** — `test_repeating_d25_after_a_crash_replays_idempotently`,\n    `test_repeating_d31_after_a_crash_replays_idempotently`,\n    `test_re_admitting_a_workbook_repair_after_the_head_already_advanced_fails_closed`,\n    `test_repeating_the_terminal_write_after_a_crash_replays_idempotently`.\n\nPlus two declared structural gaps (`test_blocked_d05_cannot_reach_d24_yet`,\n`test_blocked_d91_cannot_reach_d29_yet`), owned by `N30_UNIT_GRAPH`.\n\n## Known scope limitations (for N40 and future generations)\n\n- **D24 is unreachable from `D05_SELECT_NEXT_UNIT`**, and **`D91`'s\n  `M07`/`M08`-repairable-failure branch is unreachable to `D29`**, in the\n  compiled production graph — both because `unit_graph.py`'s frozen\n  destination tables predate D24/D29's existence. Closing this is\n  `N30_UNIT_GRAPH`'s `unit_flow_or_denominator` rework edge: add\n  `\"D24_PROVE_EXACT_MANIFEST_COVERAGE\"` to `D05_SELECT_NEXT_UNIT`'s reachable\n  set (it already falls out of `routing.guard_destinations` once\n  `binding_inventory()` names D24 — the fix is in `unit_graph.py`/\n  `binding_inventory()` together, not in `routing.py`, which already has the\n  correct `GUARD_DESTINATIONS` row) and add\n  `\"D29_CLASSIFY_AND_PLAN_WORKBOOK_REPAIR\"` to\n  `unit_graph.MODEL_BRANCH_DESTINATIONS[\"D91_CLASSIFY_MODEL_FAILURE\"]`.\n  N40_CLI_CUTOVER cannot ship a real `mode=all` run until this closes.\n- **D16-D23 remain ungraphed**, exactly as N31 left them; this generation did\n  not need them for D24-D32's own correctness and did not touch them.\n- The workbook assembler/inspector surface (`transport_registry\n  .assemble_workbook` / `.inspect_workbook_pages`) has no production\n  implementation yet, mirroring N30's own documented gap for\n  `render_unit`/`inspect_pages` (`_StubRegistry`, finding B-8): this\n  generation's tests supply a real, file-backed test double; N13's transport\n  registry does not yet expose either method.\n- `test_plan26_topology.py`'s `